WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.399
Week two.

00:00:01.449 --> 00:00:06.216
Market research and consumer insights, with Estelle Gohil from Fiftyfive5.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.949
Behavioural data tells you what happened.

00:00:08.999 --> 00:00:11.069
Qualitative research tells you why.

00:00:11.119 --> 00:00:13.912
And the why decides what the business does next.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.979
Say is not do.

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:18.401
A shopper says, I want something cheaper.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.606
Keep asking why,

00:00:19.656 --> 00:00:21.247
and the real driver might be value,

00:00:21.297 --> 00:00:22.097
convenience,

00:00:22.112 --> 00:00:23.532
or saving time.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.326
Research drives growth three ways.

00:00:26.376 --> 00:00:28.045
Identify where to play.

00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:31.549
Execute, through positioning, pricing and creative.

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:33.621
Then evaluate performance.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.924
The toolkit has two modes.

00:00:35.974 --> 00:00:40.266
Talking: discussion groups, consumer juries, cognitive interviews.

00:00:40.316 --> 00:00:44.417
And watching: shopping safaris, or body cameras on baristas.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.041
Gen AI helps, but it can't close three gaps.

00:00:48.091 --> 00:00:50.162
Human and cultural understanding.

00:00:50.212 --> 00:00:52.048
Data that doesn't exist yet.

00:00:52.098 --> 00:00:53.811
And the analysis itself.

00:00:53.861 --> 00:00:55.769
Keep a human in the lead.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:57.444
The takeaway?

00:00:57.494 --> 00:01:00.045
Understand people, don't just collect data.

00:01:00.095 --> 00:01:03.311
An insight only counts when it enables a decision.
